The issue title says "Context menu does not close when secondary menu opens or secondary menu should not open". The phrasing is ambiguous and likely a GitHub issue where the "secondary menu" refers to something specific on mobile - maybe the "secondary menu" is the context menu opened by right-click / long press? Hmm.

Actually, wait. In Expensify, there's a concept of "context menu". The issue says "Right click to open the secondary menu" - secondary interaction = right click. So "secondary menu" = context menu.

Actually the real issue could be about the ReportActionContextMenu not closing when a new one is requested. Looking at `showContextMenu` in ReportActionContextMenu.ts:

```js
// If there is an already open context menu, close it first before opening
// a new one.
if (contextMenuRef.current.instanceID) {
    hideContextMenu(false, show);
    return;
}

show();
```

This looks like the fix is already there. Hmm.

